rem Exploring Pascal's Pyramid
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=154
rem Count the entries of row N of
rem Pascal's pyramid, the multinomial
rem coefficients N! / (i! j! k!), that
rem are multiples of 10^Power

use sequences
use io
use cli

option N integer = 200000
option Power integer = 12

rem The exponent of p in N! / (i! j! k!)
rem is v(N) - v(i) - v(j) - v(k), with
rem v(m) the exponent of p in m!, from
rem Legendre's sums. Walk the triples
rem i <= j <= k, weighing each by its
rem arrangements. The exponent of 5 in
rem C(N, i) must be at least Power minus
rem the base 5 digits of N, so most i
rem are skipped.
Rows = N + 1
Col = (0 to N array) reshape Rows 1
Up5 = 5 ** (1 to 12 array)
Up2 = 2 ** (1 to 40 array)
F5 = (Col // Up5) sum axis 1
F2 = (Col // Up2) sum axis 1
F5 = F5 copy
F2 = F2 copy
Lim5 = F5 N - Power
Lim2 = F2 N - Power
Up = 5 ** (0 to 30 array)
Digits = (Up at most N) count
Mid = N // 3
Ids = 0 to Mid array
Back = F5 N - F5 Ids - (F5 reverse) Ids
Floor = Power - Digits
Keep = Back at least Floor
Is = Ids filter Keep array
Answer = 0
for I in Is
  M = N - I
  L5 = Lim5 - F5 I
  L2 = Lim2 - F2 I
  for J in I to M // 2
    K = M - J
    if F5 J + F5 K at most L5
      if F2 J + F2 K at most L2
        W = 6
        if I equal J or J equal K
          W = 3
        end
        if I equal J and J equal K
          W = 1
        end
        Answer += W
      end
    end
  end
end
Answer print
